# bSecured server configuration. All values are optional; the server reads them
# from the environment. There are no secrets here — the server stores no keys,
# and the prototype uses an in-memory store (data is lost on restart).
#
# The server is HTTP by default. To serve HTTPS (needed for the guard's TLS pin
# check), set both of these to a certificate and its key:
# BSEC_TLS_CERT=dev-cert.pem
# BSEC_TLS_KEY=dev-key.pem

# BSEC_HOST=127.0.0.1
# BSEC_PORT=8000
# BSEC_MAX_BODY_BYTES=8192
